+# Noncollinear / Relativistic RCP: implementation status and design
+
+Target: CP2K 2026.2, `rcp-development` (starting at `c12ea981ea`).
+
+## Terminology and implemented scope
+
+| Calculation | CP2K electronic-structure representation | Current RCP status |
+|---|---|---|
+| GPW RKS / collinear UKS | Real AO, Γ point | Previously implemented and tested |
+| GPW RKS / collinear UKS k-point | Complex Bloch AO, spin channels diagonal | Previously implemented and tested |
+| Two-component noncollinear spinor **local kernel** | Complex Pauli spinor values and derivatives on grid | **Implemented** as `src/rcp_spinor.F` |
+| Fully integrated noncollinear GPW RCP | Spinor SCF and four complex AO spin blocks | **Not implemented** |
+| SOC-corrected GPW RCP | Second-variational SOC spinors from post-SCF bands | **Not connected** to the RCP output |
+| GAPW all-electron scalar relativistic ZORA or DKH | Spin-independent modified one-electron Hamiltonian | **Not implemented** in all-electron RCP, fails early with clear error |
+| PW_DFT with SIRIUS noncollinear SOC | SIRIUS spinor PW representation | **Not connected** to Quickstep RCP |
+| Four-component Dirac RCP / axial chirality | Four-component bispinor, small components | **Not implemented** |
+
+The new pure Fortran routine `rcp_spinor_local` evaluates spinor charge,
+magnetization and the same *nonrelativistic spatial derivative* kinetic/regional
+energy convention as the original scalar RCP, assuming its input spinors and
+derivatives are already evaluated at one point.
+It does **not** silently claim a relativistic kinetic-energy density.
+
+The tests cover collinear reduction, a spinor polarized along +y,
+global U(1) invariance and a global SU(2) spin rotation from +y to +x. Run:
+
+```bash
+cd ~/work/cp2k-rcp
+gfortran -ffree-form -ffree-line-length-none -Wall -fcheck=all \
+  -J local-sham/relativistic_rcp_validation/analysis \
+  src/rcp_spinor.F tests/QS/regtest-rcp/test_spinor_kernel.f90 \
+  -o local-sham/relativistic_rcp_validation/analysis/test_spinor
+local-sham/relativistic_rcp_validation/analysis/test_spinor
+```
+
+## Noncollinear window density
+
+For 2-component Bloch spinors, define at each k-point:
+
+```text
+P_{mu,nu}^{sigma,sigma'}(R) =
+ sum_{n,k} w_k W_nk c_{mu,n,k}^{sigma}
+ conj(c_{nu,n,k}^{sigma'}) exp(i k.R)
+```
+
+There are four spin blocks (uu, ud, du, dd). Hermiticity enforces
+`P_du = P_ud^dagger` with the appropriate reversed lattice image. A
+collinear UKS treatment with only uu and dd cannot describe arbitrary
+noncollinear magnetization.
+
+At a grid point,
+
+```text
+n = rho_uu + rho_dd
+m_x = rho_ud + rho_du = 2 Re(rho_ud)
+m_y = i(rho_ud - rho_du) = -2 Im(rho_ud)
+m_z = rho_uu - rho_dd
+```
+
+In the actual local implementation `rho_{sigma,sigma'}=psi_sigma conj(psi_sigma')`,
+hence `m_y = 2 Im(conj(psi_up) psi_down)`. Keep spin-density index
+ordering consistent when constructing P and mapping to the Pauli matrices.
+
+For the scalar energy numerator use the spin trace of
+the symmetric Laplacian form and the positive gradient form:
+
+```text
+t_L = -1/2 Re sum_nk w_k W_nk psi_nk^dagger (laplacian psi_nk)
+t_G = +1/2 sum_nk w_k W_nk |grad psi_nk|^2
+eps_tau,EW = -(t_L + t_G)/2
+mu_R^tau = eps_tau,EW / n_EW (with density cutoff)
+```
+
+These expressions reproduce the existing CP2K RCP implementation and
+are invariant under a constant SU(2) spin-frame rotation. They are not
+yet the local kinetic-energy density derived from a Dirac/Pauli SOC
+Hamiltonian: SO terms and spin currents require an explicit convention.
+
+## CP2K interfaces that need extensions
+
+1. **Data source:** The GPW/Quickstep `qs_rho_type` and `kpoint_env_type%mos`
+   contain either collinear spin channels, not general self-consistent 2-spin
+   eigenspinors. CP2K has second-variational SOC machinery in
+   `post_scf_bandstructure_utils.F`, including `cfm_spinor_wf_ikp`.
+   Implement an explicit interface supplying spinor eigenvalues, occupations,
+   and spinor coefficients at each k point. Distinguish SOC treated only
+   post-SCF from self-consistent spinor XC.
+2. **Complex spin-density lattice transform:** Extend the existing
+   `kpoint_density_transform` concept to all uu/ud/du/dd blocks and
+   preserve Bloch phases, complex conjugation and hermiticity across
+   lattice-image reversal. Spinful time reversal must be handled
+   explicitly; ordinary collinear symmetry averaging is insufficient.
+3. **Spin-dependent real-space collocation:** The current
+   `calculate_rho_elec` accepts a scalar density matrix (real images
+   after k→R). To obtain all Cartesian spin densities, support
+   off-diagonal complex AO-spin blocks or directly collocate spinor
+   wavefunctions and their first/second derivatives. Then call the new
+   pure `rcp_spinor_local` kernel on each grid point and write four
+   density cubes and the regional-energy cubes.
+4. **Relativistic operators:** For scalar relativistic ZORA/DKH GAPW,
+   Quickstep uses `ORB_SOFT` grid task lists plus one-center atomic
+   corrections. Reusing the GPW `calculate_rho_elec` on all-electron
+   data currently trips an assertion. An approximation using soft-only
+   density would not be equal to full GAPW all-electron RCP. Implement
+   hard corrections to n and the relativistic kinetic-energy numerator
+   before advertising ZORA/DKH support.
+5. **Physical validation:** Require checks of
+   spin-frame covariance, spin trace agreement with collinear RCP,
+   Hermiticity, k-point full-grid/symmetry agreement, integrated
+   magnetization, and scalar/relativistic limiting behavior.
+
+## Independent source-level findings
+
+- `src/qs_update_s_mstruct.F`: GAPW builds `task_list_soft` and intentionally
+  does not build `task_list` for a full `ORB` grid collocation.
+- `src/qs_core_matrices.F`: relativistic corrections modify the
+  kinetic-energy matrix; the original GPW Laplacian-grid energy is
+  therefore not generally the full relativistic kinetic energy.
+- `src/post_scf_bandstructure_utils.F`: SOC spinor eigenvectors
+  exist for post-SCF band-structure analysis but are not the same as the
+  scalar SCF density used by the existing RCP.
+- `src/input_cp2k_pwdft.F`: optional SIRIUS engine supports noncollinear
+  and SOC calculations, but not through the Quickstep RCP interface.
+
+## Failed tests that led to the guard
+
+Inputs and CP2K outputs for a GAPW H2O ZORA and DKH run are retained under
+`local-sham/relativistic_rcp_validation/`. Both original SCFs converged in
+14 steps but the old RCP path failed at `qs_collocate_density.F:1820`
+due to the unavailable non-soft task list. After adding the guard, an
+explicit error replaces the obscure assertion. This is a **known missing
+feature**, not a validated physical relativistic RCP calculation.
